# oxfmt exclusions that are THIS repo's, deliberately kept out of `.oxfmtrc.json`.
#
# `.oxfmtrc.json` is vendored byte-for-byte from its canonical copy and pinned by
# tools/vendored-config-drift.test.ts, so a repo-specific path cannot go in it without
# forking the shared floor. oxfmt reads `.gitignore` and `.prettierignore` from its cwd by
# default, which makes this the seam.
#
# What is NOT here, because tools/format.sh excludes it by construction: crates/, xtask/,
# Cargo.toml, deny.toml, schema/, .github/ and the vendored tools/oxlint-config/ are
# simply not among the paths the formatter is given. oxfmt formats TOML and YAML natively,
# so a blacklist would have to stay ahead of every new root file — it already missed
# deny.toml, which oxfmt offered to rewrite. Naming the two Bun projects positionally
# cannot miss.
#
# Everything below is INSIDE site/ or contracts/ and therefore does need naming.

# Generated by `cargo run -p xtask -- contract` and diffed byte-for-byte by CI
# (`contract --check`, and `git diff --exit-code contracts/goldens-ts`). A formatter must
# never touch a file whose bytes are the contract: reformatting it reds the gate with no
# source change, and the only real fix would be in the Rust generator.
contracts/bindings.ts
contracts/goldens/
contracts/goldens-ts/
contracts/signal-theme.json

# Lint configs are excluded as a class, not because they would break. The vendored ones
# under tools/oxlint-config/ are byte-pinned against their canonical copies and MUST NOT be
# reflowed; formatting the repo-local ones anyway would leave two classes of the same file
# type, where whether your comment block survives depends on which directory it sits in.
# Their content is load-bearing prose about traps, and it stays as authored.
**/.oxlintrc.json

# The vendored design-token contract and validator, byte-pinned against their canonical
# copies by tools/vendored-config-drift.test.ts — the same rule as tools/oxlint-config/
# above, but this one DOES need naming because it sits inside the `site` tree the formatter
# is given. They conform to this repo's oxfmt today, which is precisely why the exclusion
# looks redundant: the day upstream style and this config disagree, `--check` reds with no
# source change here and `format.sh` in write mode silently breaks the byte-pin.
site/tools/design-tokens/

# The docs mirror is sha256-pinned three ways by site/scripts/check-doc-freshness.ts.
# Reformatting an .mdx page changes its registered bytes and reds the freshness gate
# against a source that never moved. (`**/*.md` is already excluded upstream in
# .oxfmtrc.json; .mdx is not, which is why this line exists.)
site/content/
